would eventually finish 39th, while Kipchoge dropped out, his first ever DNF in a marathon."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Tola protected his lead on the steep descents, as Belgian " [:a {:href "/athletes/132653"} "Bashir Abdi"] " gave chase but never really closed on Tola. Tola would win gold in an Olympic record 2-06:26, giving him a 21-second margin over Abdi. Behind Abdi, " [:a {:href "/athletes/150263"} "Benson Kipruto"] " (KEN), who had won major marathons in Boston, Chicago, and Tokyo in the last three years, closed fastest to take the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button327116", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button327116').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "5 km"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "10 km"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "15 km"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "20 km"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Half-Marathon"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "25 km"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "30 km"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "35 km"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "40 km"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "622"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133746"} "Tamirat Tola"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ETH"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ETH.png"}] "ETH"]] [:td {} "2-06:26"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "15:42 (22)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "31:01 (27)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "46:03 (21)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "1-01:43 (2)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "1-04:51 (1)"] [:td {:class "split",